onsider negative ranges? Not needed. But we can implement robust. Let''s modify solution.py accordingly.\\"}],\\"tool_calls\\":[{\\"index\\":0,\\"type\\":\\"function\\",\\"id\\":\\"fc_4e47108e-6005-4cc5-806c-e1017247eaa8\\",\\"function\\":{\\"name\\":\\"write_file\\",\\"arguments\\":\\"{\\\\\\"content\\\\\\":\\\\\\"def sum_range(start, end):\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Return the sum of all integers from start to end, both inclusive.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    The original implementation used ``range(start, end)`` which excludes the\\\\\\\\n    ``end`` value.  The tests expect the inclusive behaviour, so we need to\\\\\\\\n    iterate up to ``end`` *inclusive*.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    ``range`` is efficient for positive steps, but if ``start`` is greater than\\\\\\\\n    ``end`` the original code would return ``0``.  The function now handles\\\\\\\\n    that case by swapping the bounds so that the sum is always computed\\\\\\\\n    correctly regardless of the order of the arguments.\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    # Ensure we iterate from the smaller to the larger value.\\\\\\\\n    if start \\\\\\\\u003e end:\\\\\\\\n        start, end = end, start\\\\\\\\n    total = 0\\\\\\\\n    for n in range(start, end + 1):\\\\\\\\n        total += n\\\\\\\\n    return total\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\",\\\\\\"path\\\\\\":\\\\\\"solution.py\\\\\\"}\\"}}],\\"reasoning_content\\":\\"Only tests for small range and single value. But we should also consider negative ranges? Not needed. But we can implement robust. Let''s modify solution.py accordingly.\\"}}],\\"created\\":1794726060,\\"model\\":\\"openai/gpt-oss-20b\\",\\"object\\":\\"chat.completion\\",\\"service_tier\\":\\"on_demand\\",\\"system_fingerprint\\":\\"fp_ce54c53bd5\\",\\"usage\\":{\\"prompt_tokens\\":603,\\"completion_tokens\\":261,\\"completion_tokens_details\\":{\\"reasoning_tokens\\":33},\\"total_tokens\\":864},\\"extra_fields\\":{\\"request_type\\":\\"chat_completion\\