t. Let''s patch solution.py.\\",\\"reasoning_details\\":[{\\"index\\":0,\\"type\\":\\"reasoning.text\\",\\"text\\":\\"Only tests for small range and single value. But we should also consider negative ranges? Not needed. But we can implement robust. Let''s patch solution.py.\\"}],\\"tool_calls\\":[{\\"index\\":0,\\"type\\":\\"function\\",\\"id\\":\\"fc_bae74f60-eacc-453a-a7cb-84a4b0e0a2b4\\",\\"function\\":{\\"name\\":\\"write_file\\",\\"arguments\\":\\"{\\\\\\"content\\\\\\":\\\\\\"def sum_range(start, end):\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Return the sum of all integers from start to end, both inclusive.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    The original implementation used ``range(start, end)`` which excludes the\\\\\\\\n    ``end`` value.  This caused the function to return the wrong result for\\\\\\\\n    ranges where ``start`` and ``end`` are different and for the trivial case\\\\\\\\n    where ``start == end``.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    The corrected implementation uses ``range(start, end + 1)`` so that the\\\\\\\\n    upper bound is included.  It also works correctly when ``start`` is\\\\\\\\n    greater than ``end`` by swapping the values \\u2013 this makes the function\\\\\\\\n    more robust and easier to reason about.\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    # Ensure the range is in ascending order.\\\\\\\\n    if start \\\\\\\\u003e end:\\\\\\\\n        start, end = end, start\\\\\\\\n    total = 0\\\\\\\\n    for n in range(start, end + 1):\\\\\\\\n        total += n\\\\\\\\n    return total\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\",\\\\\\"path\\\\\\":\\\\\\"solution.py\\\\\\"}\\"}}],\\"reasoning_content\\":\\"Only tests for small range and single value. But we should also consider negative ranges? Not needed. But we can implement robust. Let''s patch solution.py.\\"}}],\\"created\\":1794727225,\\"model\\":\\"openai/gpt-oss-20b\\",\\"object\\":\\"chat.completion\\",\\"service_tier\\":\\"on_demand\\",\\"system_fingerprint\\":\\"fp_996f667773\\",\\"u